From: Vladimir Skvortsov <vskvortsov@emcraft.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: imx6sx-sdb-reva: reset through the internal path

imx6sx-sdb.dtsi marks wdog1 fsl,ext-reset-output, so imx2_wdt_restart()
sets WCR[SRS] to suppress the internal reset and drives WDOG_B instead.
The only watchdog pad the board muxes is WDOG1_WDOG_ANY, and on RevA
nothing that pad reaches resets the system: reboot(8) leaves the kernel
at "Reboot failed -- System halted" until the watchdog times out roughly
two minutes later and resets the board itself.

Both internal reset paths work on this silicon. U-Boot resets it
immediately, because reset_cpu() calls imx_watchdog_expire_now(wdog,
false) unconditionally, and the watchdog timeout resets it as well.
Only the software-asserted external path is dead.

Drop the property on RevA alone, so the kernel takes the same internal
path. RevB and later keep the external reset, which also cycles the
PMIC.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Vladimir Skvortsov <vskvortsov@emcraft.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/nxp/imx/imx6sx-sdb-reva.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/nxp/imx/imx6sx-sdb-reva.dts
@@ -167,3 +167,8 @@
 &snvs_pwrkey {
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+/* WDOG_ANY does not reset this revision; reboot through the internal path. */
+&wdog1 {
+	/delete-property/ fsl,ext-reset-output;
+};
